      "type": "nw-story",
      "name": "NW Story",
      "settings": {
        "text_column_left": "<p>That reaction sent them looking into the category properly. What they found was a gap nobody had bothered to close.</p><p>Together they bring more than 15 years of e-commerce experience, and 9 years as hands-on parents living the missing-sock, mismatched-drawer, low-key family sock wars chaos that most households will recognise instantly.</p><p>Before having children, Liz spent a decade as a physiotherapist and Pilates instructor. She used that genuine, technical understanding of foot biomechanics to lead development of the Pearler sock, and more specifically the AirMap System. Not a marketing approximation of it.</p>",
        "text_column_right": "<p>Three manufacturers told them it couldn't be done, because that's not how the sock industry works. Two more started on the idea, then said it was too hard. Then they found the team, locally in Melbourne, who said YES.</p><p>Three years and 56 samples later, here we are.</p>",
